Column name: rent_25_to_30_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 25 to 29.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 25.0 to 29.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_20_to_25_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 20 to 24.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 20.0 to 24.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_15_to_20_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 15 to 19.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 15.0 to 19.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_10_to_15_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending 10 to 14.9% income on rent. Gross rent from 10.0 to 14.9 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: rent_under_10_percent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units spending less than 10% on rent. Gross rent less than 10 percent of household income. Computed ratio of monthly gross rent to monthly household income (total household income divided by 12). The ratio is computed separately for each unit and is rounded to the nearest tenth. Units for which no rent is paid and units occupied by households that report no income or a net loss comprise the category, "Not computed". Gross rent as a percentage of household income provides information on the monthly housing cost expenses for renters. 
Column name: total_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Total Population. The total number of all people living in a given geographic area.  This is a very useful catch-all denominator when calculating rates.
Column name: male_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male Population. The number of people within each geography who are male.
Column name: female_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female Population. The number of people within each geography who are female.
Column name: median_age Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Age. The median age of all people in a given geographic area.
Column name: white_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: White Population. The number of people identifying as white, non-Hispanic in each geography.
Column name: black_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Black or African American Population. The number of people identifying as black or African American, non-Hispanic in each geography.
Column name: asian_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Asian Population. The number of people identifying as Asian, non-Hispanic in each geography.
Column name: hispanic_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Hispanic Population. The number of people identifying as Hispanic or Latino in each geography.
Column name: amerindian_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: American Indian and Alaska Native Population. The number of people identifying as American Indian or Alaska native in each geography.
Column name: other_race_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Other Race population. The number of people identifying as another race in each geography
Column name: two_or_more_races_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two or more races population. The number of people identifying as two or more races in each geography
Column name: not_hispanic_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population not Hispanic. The number of people not identifying as Hispanic or Latino in each geography.
Column name: commuters_by_public_transportation Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters by Public Transportation. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily traveled to work by public transportation.  This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance, by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get from home to work.
Column name: households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households. A count of the number of households in each geography. A household consists of one or more people who live in the same dwelling and also share at meals or living accommodation, and may consist of a single family or some other grouping of people. 
Column name: median_income Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Household Income in the past 12 Months. Within a geographic area, the median income received by every household on a regular basis before payments for personal income taxes, social security, union dues, medicare deductions, etc.  It includes income received from wages, salary, commissions, bonuses, and tips; self-employment income from own nonfarm or farm businesses, including proprietorships and partnerships; interest, dividends, net rental income, royalty income, or income from estates and trusts; Social Security or Railroad Retirement income; Supplemental Security Income (SSI); any cash public assistance or welfare payments from the state or local welfare office; retirement, survivor, or disability benefits; and any other sources of income received regularly such as Veterans' (VA) payments, unemployment and/or worker's compensation, child support, and alimony.
Column name: income_per_capita Type: FLOAT64 Description: Per Capita Income in the past 12 Months. Per capita income is the mean income computed for every man, woman, and child in a particular group. It is derived by dividing the total income of a particular group by the total population.
Column name: housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing Units. A count of housing units in each geography.  A housing unit is a house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters.
Column name: vacant_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Vacant Housing Units. The count of vacant housing units in a geographic area. A housing unit is vacant if no one is living in it at the time of enumeration, unless its occupants are only temporarily absent. Units temporarily occupied at the time of enumeration entirely by people who have a usual residence elsewhere are also classified as vacant.
Column name: vacant_housing_units_for_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Vacant Housing Units for Rent. The count of vacant housing units in a geographic area that are for rent. A housing unit is vacant if no one is living in it at the time of enumeration, unless its occupants are only temporarily absent. Units temporarily occupied at the time of enumeration entirely by people who have a usual residence elsewhere are also classified as vacant.
Column name: vacant_housing_units_for_sale Type: FLOAT64 Description: Vacant Housing Units for Sale. The count of vacant housing units in a geographic area that are for sale. A housing unit is vacant if no one is living in it at the time of enumeration, unless its occupants are only temporarily absent. Units temporarily occupied at the time of enumeration entirely by people who have a usual residence elsewhere are also classified as vacant.
Column name: median_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Median Rent. The median contract rent within a geographic area. The contract rent is the monthly rent agreed to or contracted for, regardless of any furnishings, utilities, fees, meals, or services that may be included. For vacant units, it is the monthly rent asked for the rental unit at the time of interview.
Column name: percent_income_spent_on_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Percent of Household Income Spent on Rent. Within a geographic area, the median percentage of household income which was spent on gross rent.  Gross rent is the amount of the contract rent plus the estimated average monthly cost of utilities (electricity, gas, water, sewer etc.) and fuels (oil, coal, wood, etc.) if these are paid by the renter.  Household income is the sum of the income of all people 15 years and older living in the household.
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-occupied Housing Units
Column name: million_dollar_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-occupied Housing Units valued at $1,000,000 or more.. The count of owner occupied housing units in a geographic area that are valued at $1,000,000 or more.  Value is the respondent's estimate of how much the property (house and lot, mobile home and lot, or condominium unit) would sell for if it were for sale.
Column name: mortgaged_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-occupied Housing Units with a Mortgage. The count of housing units within a geographic area that are mortagaged. "Mortgage" refers to all forms of debt where the property is pledged as security for repayment of the debt, including deeds of trust, trust deed, contracts to purchase, land contracts, junior mortgages, and home equity loans.
Column name: families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Families with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, both parents in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_father_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, father only in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_mother_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, mother only in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: two_parents_not_in_labor_force_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-parent families, neither parent in labor force with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: one_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: One-parent families with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: father_one_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: One-parent families, father, with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: father_in_labor_force_one_parent_families_with_young_children Type: FLOAT64 Description: One-parent families, father in labor force, with young children (under 6 years of age)
Column name: commute_10_14_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 10 and 14 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 10 and 14 minutes. 
Column name: commute_15_19_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 15 and 19 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 15 and 19 minutes. 
Column name: commute_20_24_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 20 and 24 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 20 and 24 minutes.
Column name: commute_25_29_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 25 and 29 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 25 and 29 minutes. 
Column name: commute_30_34_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 30 and 34 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 30 and 34 minutes. 
Column name: commute_45_59_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 45 and 59 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 45 and 59 minutes. 
Column name: aggregate_travel_time_to_work Type: FLOAT64 Description: Aggregate travel time to work. The total number of minutes every worker in a geographic area over the age of 16 who did not work from home spent spent commuting to work in one day
Column name: income_less_10000 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income less than $10,000. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was less than $10,000.
Column name: income_10000_14999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $10,000 to $14,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $10,000 and $14,999.
Column name: income_15000_19999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $15,000 to $19,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $15,000 and $19,999.
Column name: income_20000_24999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $20,000 to $24,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $20,000 and $24,999.
Column name: income_25000_29999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $25,000 to $29,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $20,000 and $24,999.
Column name: income_30000_34999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $30,000 to $34,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $30,000 and $34,999.
Column name: income_35000_39999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $35,000 to $39,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $35,000 and $39,999.
Column name: income_40000_44999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $40,000 to $44,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $40,000 and $44,999.
Column name: income_45000_49999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $45,000 to $49,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $45,000 and $49,999.
Column name: income_50000_59999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $50,000 to $59,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $50,000 and $59,999.
Column name: income_60000_74999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $60,000 to $74,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $60,000 and $74,999.
Column name: income_75000_99999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $75,000 to $99,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $75,000 and $99,999.
Column name: income_100000_124999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $100,000 to $124,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $100,000 and $124,999.
Column name: income_125000_149999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $125,000 to $149,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $125,000 and $149,999.
Column name: income_150000_199999 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $150,000 to $199,999. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was between $150,000 and $1999,999.
Column name: income_200000_or_more Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with income of $200,000 Or More. The number of households in a geographic area whose annual income was more than $200,000.
Column name: renter_occupied_housing_units_paying_cash_median_gross_rent Type: FLOAT64 Description: Renter-Occupied Housing Units Paying Cash Rent Median Gross Rent
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units_lower_value_quartile Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-Occupied Housing Units Lower Value Quartile
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units_median_value Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-Occupied Housing Units Median Value. The middle value (median) in a geographic area owner occupied housing units.
Column name: owner_occupied_housing_units_upper_value_quartile Type: FLOAT64 Description: Owner-Occupied Housing Units Upper Value Quartile
Column name: married_households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Married households. People in formal marriages, as well as people in common-law marriages, are included. Does not include same-sex marriages.
Column name: occupied_housing_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Occupied housing units. A housing unit is classified as occupied if it is the usual place of residence of the person or group of people living in it at the time of enumeration.
Column name: housing_units_renter_occupied Type: FLOAT64 Description: Renter occupied housing units. All occupied units which are not owner occupied, whether they are rented for cash rent or occupied without payment of cash rent, are classified as renter-occupied.
Column name: dwellings_1_units_detached Type: FLOAT64 Description: Single-family (one unit) detached dwellings. This is a 1-unit structure detached from any other house, that is, with open space on all four sides. Such structures are considered detached even if they have an adjoining shed or garage. A one-family house that contains a business is considered detached as long as the building has open space on all four sides. Mobile homes to which one or more permanent rooms have been added or built also are included.
Column name: dwellings_1_units_attached Type: FLOAT64 Description: Single-family (one unit) attached dwellings. This is a 1-unit structure that has one or more walls extending from ground to roof separating it from adjoining structures. In row houses (sometimes called townhouses), double houses, or houses attached to nonresidential structures, each house is a separate, attached structure if the dividing or common wall goes from ground to roof.
Column name: dwellings_2_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two-family (two unit) dwellings
Column name: dwellings_3_to_4_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Multifamily dwellings with three to 4 units
Column name: dwellings_5_to_9_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 5 to 9 units
Column name: dwellings_10_to_19_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 10 to 19 units
Column name: dwellings_20_to_49_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 20 to 49 units
Column name: dwellings_50_or_more_units Type: FLOAT64 Description: Apartment buildings with 50 or more units
Column name: mobile_homes Type: FLOAT64 Description: Mobile homes. A manufactured home is defined as a movable dwelling, 8 feet or more wide and 40 feet or more long, designed to be towed on its own chassis, with transportation gear integral to the unit when it leaves the factory, and without need of a permanent foundation. These homes are built in accordance with the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) building code.
Column name: housing_built_2005_or_later Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units built in 2005 or later. A house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters built in 2005 or later.
Column name: housing_built_2000_to_2004 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units built between 2000 and 2004. A house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters built from 2000 to 2004.
Column name: housing_built_1939_or_earlier Type: FLOAT64 Description: Housing units built before 1939. A house, an apartment, a mobile home or trailer, a group of rooms, or a single room occupied as separate living quarters, or if vacant, intended for occupancy as separate living quarters built in 1939 or earlier.
Column name: male_under_5 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male under 5 years. The male population over the age of five years within the specified area.
Column name: male_5_to_9 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 5 to 9. The male population between the age of five years to nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_10_to_14 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 10 to 14. The male population between the age of ten years to fourteen years within the specified area.
Column name: male_15_to_17 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 15 to 17. The male population between the age of fifteeen years to seventeen years within the specified area.
Column name: male_18_to_19 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 18 and 19. The male population between the age of eighteen years to nineteen years within the specified area.
Column name: male_20 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 20. The male population with an age of twenty years within the specified area.
Column name: male_21 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 21. The male population with an age of twenty-one years within the specified area.
Column name: male_22_to_24 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 22 to 24. The male population between the age of twenty-two years to twenty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_25_to_29 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 25 to 29. The male population between the age of twenty-five years to twenty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_30_to_34 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 30 to 34. The male population between the age of thirty years to thirty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_35_to_39 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 35 to 39. The male population between the age of thirty-five years to thirty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_40_to_44 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 40 to 44. The male population between the age of fourty years to fourty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_45_to_49 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 49. The male population between the age of fourty-five years to fourty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_50_to_54 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 50 to 54. The male population between the age of fifty years to fifty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_55_to_59 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 55 to 59. The male population between the age of fifty-five years to fifty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_60_61 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 60 to 61. The male population between the age of sixty years to sixty-one years within the specified area.
Column name: male_62_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 62 to 64. The male population between the age of sixty-two years to sixty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_65_to_66 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 65 to 66. The male population between the age of sixty-five years to sixty-six years within the specified area.
Column name: male_67_to_69 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 67 to 69. The male population between the age of sixty-seven years to sixty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_70_to_74 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 70 to 74. The male population between the age of seventy years to seventy-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_75_to_79 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 75 to 79. The male population between the age of seventy-five years to seventy-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: male_80_to_84 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 80 to 84. The male population between the age of eighty years to eighty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_85_and_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Male age 85 and over. The male population of the age of eighty-five years and over within the specified area.
Column name: female_under_5 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female under 5 years. The female population over the age of five years within the specified area.
Column name: female_5_to_9 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 5 to 9. The female population between the age of five years to nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_10_to_14 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 10 to 14. The female population between the age of ten years to fourteen years within the specified area.
Column name: female_15_to_17 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 15 to 17. The female population between the age of fifteeen years to seventeen years within the specified area.
Column name: female_18_to_19 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 18 and 19. The female population between the age of eighteen years to nineteen years within the specified area.
Column name: female_20 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 20. The female population with an age of twenty years within the specified area.
Column name: female_21 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 21. The female population with an age of twenty-one years within the specified area.
Column name: female_22_to_24 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 22 to 24. The female population between the age of twenty-two years to twenty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_25_to_29 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 25 to 29. The female population between the age of twenty-five years to twenty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_30_to_34 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 30 to 34. The female population between the age of thirty years to thirty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_35_to_39 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 35 to 39. The female population between the age of thirty-five years to thirty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_40_to_44 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 40 to 44. The female population between the age of fourty years to fourty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_45_to_49 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 45 to 49. The female population between the age of fourty-five years to fourty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_50_to_54 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 50 to 54. The female population between the age of fifty years to fifty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_55_to_59 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 55 to 59. The female population between the age of fifty-five years to fifty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_60_to_61 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 60 and 61. The female population between the age of sixty years to sixty-one years within the specified area.
Column name: female_62_to_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 62 to 64. The female population between the age of sixty-two years to sixty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_65_to_66 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 65 to 66. The female population between the age of sixty-five years to sixty-six years within the specified area.
Column name: female_67_to_69 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 67 to 69. The female population between the age of sixty-seven years to sixty-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_70_to_74 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 70 to 74. The female population between the age of seventy years to seventy-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_75_to_79 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 75 to 79. The female population between the age of seventy-five years to seventy-nine years within the specified area.
Column name: female_80_to_84 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 80 to 84. The female population between the age of eighty years to eighty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: female_85_and_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Female age 85 and over. The female population of the age of eighty-five years and over within the specified area.
Column name: white_including_hispanic Type: FLOAT64 Description: White including Hispanic
Column name: black_including_hispanic Type: FLOAT64 Description: Black including Hispanic
Column name: amerindian_including_hispanic Type: FLOAT64 Description: American Indian including Hispanic
Column name: asian_including_hispanic Type: FLOAT64 Description: Asian including Hispanic
Column name: commute_5_9_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 5 and 9 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 5 and 9 minutes.
Column name: commute_35_39_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 35 and 39 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 35 and 39 minutes. 
Column name: commute_40_44_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 40 and 44 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 40 and 44 minutes. 
Column name: commute_60_89_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 60 and 89 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 60 and 89 minutes .
Column name: commute_90_more_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute of more than 90 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute more than 90 minutes.
Column name: households_retirement_income Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households receiving retirement income
Column name: armed_forces Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population in Armed Forces. The number of people in each geography who are members of the U.S. Armed Forces (people on active duty with the United States Army, Air Force, Navy, Marine Corps, or Coast Guard).
Column name: civilian_labor_force Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population in Civilian Labor Force. The number of civilians 16 years and over in each geography who can be classified as either "employed" or "unemployed" below.
Column name: employed_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Employed Population. The number of civilians 16 years old and over in each geography who either (1) were "at work," that is, those who did any work at all during the reference week as paid employees, worked in their own business or profession, worked on their own farm, or worked 15 hours or more as unpaid workers on a family farm or in a family business; or (2) were "with a job but not at work," that is, those who did not work during the reference week but had jobs or businesses from which they were temporarily absent due to illness, bad weather, industrial dispute, vacation, or other personal reasons. Excluded from the employed are people whose only activity consisted of work around the house or unpaid volunteer work for religious, charitable, and similar organizations; also excluded are all institutionalized people and people on active duty in the United States Armed Forces.
Column name: unemployed_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: 
Column name: not_in_labor_force Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population Not in Labor Force. The number of people in each geography who are 16 years old and over who are not classified as members of the labor force. This category consists mainly of students, homemakers, retired workers, seasonal workers interviewed in an off season who were not looking for work, institutionalized people, and people doing only incidental unpaid family work (less than 15 hours during the reference week).
Column name: pop_16_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population age 16 and over. The number of people in each geography who are age 16 or over.
Column name: pop_in_labor_force Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population in Labor Force. The number of people in each geography who are either in the civilian labor force or are members of the U.S. Armed Forces (people on active duty with the United States Army, Air Force, Navy, Marine Corps, or Coast Guard).
Column name: asian_male_45_54 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Asian Men age 45 to 54
Column name: asian_male_55_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Asian Men age 55 to 64
Column name: black_male_45_54 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Black Men age 45 to 54
Column name: black_male_55_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Black Men age 55 to 64
Column name: hispanic_male_45_54 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Hispanic Men age 45 to 54
Column name: hispanic_male_55_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Hispanic Men age 55 to 64
Column name: white_male_45_54 Type: FLOAT64 Description: White Men age 45 to 54
Column name: white_male_55_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: White Men age 55 to 64
Column name: bachelors_degree_2 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population who completed a bachelor's degree. From mobility table.
Column name: bachelors_degree_or_higher_25_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population with Bachelors Degree or Higher, Ages 25 to 64. The number of people in each geography who are between the ages of 25 and 64 who have attained a bachelors degree or higher. 
Column name: children Type: FLOAT64 Description: Children under 18 Years of Age. The number of people within each geography who are under 18 years of age.
Column name: children_in_single_female_hh Type: FLOAT64 Description: Children under 18 years of age in single female-led household
Column name: commuters_by_bus Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters by Bus. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily traveled to work by bus.  This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance, by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get from home to work.  This is a subset of workers who commuted by public transport.
Column name: commuters_by_car_truck_van Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters by Car, Truck, or Van. The number of workers age 16 years and over within  a geographic area who primarily traveled to work by car, truck or  van.  This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance,  by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get  from home to work.
Column name: commuters_by_carpool Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters by Carpool. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily traveled to work by carpool.  This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance, by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get from home to work.
Column name: commuters_by_subway_or_elevated Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters by Subway or Elevated. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily traveled to work by subway or elevated train.  This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance, by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get from home to work.  This is a subset of workers who commuted by public transport.
Column name: commuters_drove_alone Type: FLOAT64 Description: Commuters who drove alone. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily traveled by car driving alone. This is the principal mode of travel or type of conveyance, by distance rather than time, that the worker usually used to get from home to work.
Column name: different_house_year_ago_different_city Type: FLOAT64 Description: Lived in a different house one year ago in a different city. All people in a geographic area who lived in a different city within the year prior to the survey.
Column name: different_house_year_ago_same_city Type: FLOAT64 Description: Lived in a different house one year ago in the same city. All people in a geographic area who lived in the same city but moved to a different unit within the year prior to the survey.
Column name: employed_agriculture_forestry_fishing_hunting_mining Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in agriculture, forestry, fishing, hunting, or mining. The Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing and Hunting sector comprises establishments primarily engaged in growing crops, raising animals, harvesting timber, and harvesting fish and other animals from a farm, ranch, or their natural habitats.
Column name: employed_arts_entertainment_recreation_accommodation_food Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in arts, entertainment, recreation, accommodation and food services. The Arts, Entertainment, and Recreation sector includes a wide range of establishments that operate facilities or provide services to meet varied cultural, entertainment, and recreational interests of their patrons. This sector comprises (1) establishments that are involved in producing, promoting, or participating in live performances, events, or exhibits intended for public viewing; (2) establishments that preserve and exhibit objects and sites of historical, cultural, or educational interest; and (3) establishments that operate facilities or provide services that enable patrons to participate in recreational activities or pursue amusement, hobby, and leisure-time interests.
Column name: employed_construction Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in construction. The Construction sector comprises establishments primarily engaged in the construction of buildings or engineering projects (e.g., highways and utility systems). Construction work done may include new work, additions, alterations, or maintenance and repairs.
Column name: employed_education_health_social Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in educational services, health care, and social assistance. Outpatient health services, other than hospital care, including: public health administration; research and education; categorical health programs; treatment and immunization clinics; nursing; environmental health activities such as air and water pollution control; ambulance service if provided separately from fire protection services, and other general public health activities such as mosquito abatement. School health services provided by health agencies (rather than school agencies) are included here. Sewage treatment operations are classified under Sewerage.
Column name: employed_finance_insurance_real_estate Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in finance, insurance, real estate and rental and leasing. The Real Estate and Rental and Leasing sector comprises establishments primarily engaged in renting, leasing, or otherwise allowing the use of tangible or intangible assets, and establishments providing related services. The major portion of this sector comprises establishments that rent, lease, or otherwise allow the use of their own assets by others. The assets may be tangible, as is the case of real estate and equipment, or intangible, as is the case with patents and trademarks.
Column name: employed_information Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in information. The Information sector comprises establishments engaged in the following processes: (a) producing and distributing information and cultural products, (b) providing the means to transmit or distribute these products as well as data or communications, and (c) processing data. Included are the publishing industries, the motion picture and sound recording industries; the broadcasting industries, the telecommunications industries; Web search portals, data processing industries, and the information services industries.
Column name: employed_manufacturing Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in manufacturing. The Manufacturing sector comprises establishments engaged in the mechanical, physical, or chemical transformation of materials, substances, or components into new products.
Column name: employed_other_services_not_public_admin Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in other services except public administration. The Other Services (Except Public Administration) sector comprises establishments engaged in providing services not specifically provided for elsewhere in the classification system. Establishments in this sector are primarily engaged in activities such as equipment and machinery repairing, promoting or administering religious activities, grantmaking, advocacy, and providing drycleaning and laundry services, personal care services, death care services, pet care services, photofinishing services, temporary parking services, and dating services. Private households that engage in employing workers on or about the premises in activities primarily concerned with the operation of the household are included in this sector.
Column name: employed_public_administration Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in public administration. The Public Administration sector consists of establishments of federal, state, and local government agencies that administer, oversee, and manage public programs and have executive, legislative, or judicial authority over other institutions within a given area. These agencies also set policy, create laws, adjudicate civil and criminal legal cases, provide for public safety and for national defense. In general, government establishments in the public administration sector oversee governmental programs and activities that are not performed by private establishments.
Column name: employed_retail_trade Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in retail trade. The Retail Trade sector comprises establishments engaged in retailing merchandise, generally without transformation, and rendering services incidental to the sale of merchandise. The retailing process is the final step in the distribution of merchandise; retailers are, therefore, organized to sell merchandise in small quantities to the general public.
Column name: employed_science_management_admin_waste Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in professional scientific, management, administrative and waste management services. The Administrative and Support and Waste Management and Remediation Services sector comprises establishments performing routine support activities for the day-to-day operations of other organizations. The establishments in this sector specialize in one or more of these support activities and provide these services to clients in a variety of industries and, in some cases, to households. Activities performed include office administration, hiring and placing of personnel, document preparation and similar clerical services, solicitation, collection, security and surveillance services, cleaning, and waste disposal services.
Column name: employed_transportation_warehousing_utilities Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in transportation, warehousing, and utilities. The Transportation and Warehousing sector includes industries providing transportation of passengers and cargo, warehousing and storage for goods, scenic and sightseeing transportation, and support activities related to modes of transportation. The modes of transportation are air, rail, water, road, and pipeline.
Column name: employed_wholesale_trade Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in firms in wholesale trade. The Wholesale Trade sector comprises establishments engaged in wholesaling merchandise, generally without transformation, and rendering services incidental to the sale of merchandise. The wholesaling process is an intermediate step in the distribution of merchandise. Wholesalers are organized to sell or arrange the purchase or sale of (a) goods for resale (i.e., goods sold to other wholesalers or retailers), (b) capital or durable nonconsumer goods, and (c) raw and intermediate materials and supplies used in production.
Column name: female_female_households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with two female partners. An unmarried partner is a person age 15 years and over, who is not related to the householder, who shares living quarters, and who has an intimate relationship with the householder.
Column name: four_more_cars Type: FLOAT64 Description: Four car households. The number of households with four or more passenger cars, vans, pickup or panel trucks of one-ton capacity or less kept at home and available for the use of household members. Vehicles rented or leased for one month or more, company vehicles, and police and government vehicles are included if kept at home and used for non-business purposes. Dismantled or immobile vehicles ware excluded. Vehicles kept at home but used only for business purposes also are excluded.
Column name: gini_index Type: FLOAT64 Description: Gini Index. The Gini index, or index of income concentration, is a statistical measure of income inequality ranging from 0 to 1. A measure of 1 indicates perfect inequality, i.e., one household having all the income and rest having none. A measure of 0 indicates perfect equality, i.e., all households having an equal share of income.
Column name: graduate_professional_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population who completed a graduate or professional degree
Column name: group_quarters Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population living in group quarters
Column name: high_school_including_ged Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population with high school degree, including GED. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who attained a high school degree or GED.
Column name: households_public_asst_or_food_stamps Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households on cash public assistance or receiving food stamps (SNAP)
Column name: in_grades_1_to_4 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Students Enrolled in Grades 1 to 4. The total number of people in each geography currently enrolled in grades 1 through 4 inclusive.  This corresponds roughly to elementary school.
Column name: in_grades_5_to_8 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Students Enrolled in Grades 5 to 8. The total number of people in each geography currently enrolled in grades 5 through 8 inclusive.  This corresponds roughly to middle school.
Column name: in_grades_9_to_12 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Students Enrolled in Grades 9 to 12. The total number of people in each geography currently enrolled in grades 9 through 12 inclusive.  This corresponds roughly to high school.
Column name: in_school Type: FLOAT64 Description: Students Enrolled in School. The total number of people in each geography currently enrolled at any level of school, from nursery or pre-school to advanced post-graduate education.  Only includes those over the age of 3.
Column name: in_undergrad_college Type: FLOAT64 Description: Students Enrolled as Undergraduate in College. The number of people in a geographic area who are enrolled in college at the undergraduate level. Enrollment refers to being registered or listed as a student in an educational program leading to a college degree. This may be a public school or college, a private school or college.
Column name: less_than_high_school_graduate Type: FLOAT64 Description: Less than high school graduate. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who have not completed high school or any other advanced degree.
Column name: male_45_64_associates_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who obtained an associate's degree
Column name: male_45_64_bachelors_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who obtained a bachelor's degree
Column name: male_45_64_graduate_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who obtained a graduate or professional degree
Column name: male_45_64_less_than_9_grade Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who attained less than a 9th grade education
Column name: male_45_64_grade_9_12 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who attained between 9th and 12th grade, no diploma
Column name: male_45_64_high_school Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who completed high school or obtained GED
Column name: male_45_64_some_college Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 who completed some college, no degree
Column name: male_45_to_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Men age 45 to 64 ("middle aged"). The male population between the age of fourty-five years to sixty-four years within the specified area.
Column name: male_male_households Type: FLOAT64 Description: Households with two male partners. An unmarried partner is a person age 15 years and over, who is not related to the householder, who shares living quarters, and who has an intimate relationship with the householder.
Column name: management_business_sci_arts_employed Type: FLOAT64 Description: Civilian Employed Population in Management, Business, Science, and Arts Occupations. The number of employed civilians 16 years old and over in each geography in the Management, Business, Science, and Arts occupations. Occupation codes are based on the Standard Occupational Classification (SOC), published by the Executive Office of the President, Office of Management and Budget.
Column name: no_car Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers age 16 and over with no vehicle. All people in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not own a car.
Column name: no_cars Type: FLOAT64 Description: Car-free households. The number of households without passenger cars, vans, and pickup or panel trucks of one-ton capacity or less kept at home and available for the use of household members. Vehicles rented or leased for one month or more, company vehicles, and police and government vehicles are included if kept at home and used for non-business purposes. Dismantled or immobile vehicles ware excluded. Vehicles kept at home but used only for business purposes also are excluded.
Column name: not_us_citizen_pop Type: FLOAT64 Description: Not a U.S. Citizen Population. The number of people within each geography who indicated that they are not U.S. citizens.
Column name: occupation_management_arts Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in management business science and arts occupations
Column name: occupation_natural_resources_construction_maintenance Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in natural resources, construction, and maintenance occupations
Column name: occupation_production_transportation_material Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in production, transportation, and material moving
Column name: occupation_sales_office Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in sales and office occupations
Column name: occupation_services Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers employed in service occupations
Column name: one_car Type: FLOAT64 Description: One car households. The number of households with one passenger car, van, , pickup or panel trucks of one-ton capacity or less kept at home and available for the use of household members. Vehicles rented or leased for one month or more, company vehicles, and police and government vehicles are included if kept at home and used for non-business purposes. Dismantled or immobile vehicles ware excluded. Vehicles kept at home but used only for business purposes also are excluded.
Column name: two_cars Type: FLOAT64 Description: Two car households. The number of households with two passenger cars, vans, pickup or panel trucks of one-ton capacity or less kept at home and available for the use of household members. Vehicles rented or leased for one month or more, company vehicles, and police and government vehicles are included if kept at home and used for non-business purposes. Dismantled or immobile vehicles ware excluded. Vehicles kept at home but used only for business purposes also are excluded.
Column name: three_cars Type: FLOAT64 Description: Three car households. The number of households with one passenger cars, vans, pickup or panel trucks of one-ton capacity or less kept at home and available for the use of household members. Vehicles rented or leased for one month or more, company vehicles, and police and government vehicles are included if kept at home and used for non-business purposes. Dismantled or immobile vehicles ware excluded. Vehicles kept at home but used only for business purposes also are excluded.
Column name: pop_25_64 Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population age 25 to 64. The number of people in each geography who are between the ages of 25 and 64. 
Column name: pop_determined_poverty_status Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population for Whom Poverty Status Determined. The number of people in each geography who could be identified as either living in poverty or not.  This should be used as the denominator when calculating poverty rates, as it excludes people for whom it was not possible to determine poverty.
Column name: population_1_year_and_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population 1 year and over. All people, male and female, child and adult, living in a given geographic area that are 1 year and older.
Column name: population_3_years_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population 3 Years and Over. The total number of people in each geography age 3 years and over.  This denominator is mostly used to calculate rates of school enrollment.
Column name: poverty Type: FLOAT64 Description: Income In The Past 12 Months Below Poverty Level. The number of people in a geographic area who are part of a family (which could be just them as an individual) determined to be "in poverty" following the Office of Management and Budget's Directive 14. (https://www.census.gov/hhes/povmeas/methodology/ombdir14.html)
Column name: sales_office_employed Type: FLOAT64 Description: Civilian Employed Population in Sales and Office Occupations. The number of employed civilians 16 years old and over in each geography in the Sales and Office occupations. Occupation codes are based on the Standard Occupational Classification (SOC), published by the Executive Office of the President, Office of Management and Budget.
Column name: some_college_and_associates_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population who completed some college or obtained associate's degree. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who obtained an associate's degree, and did not complete a more advanced degree.
Column name: walked_to_work Type: FLOAT64 Description: Walked to Work. The number of workers age 16 years and over within a geographic area who primarily walked to work.  This would mean that of any way of getting to work, they travelled the most distance walking.
Column name: worked_at_home Type: FLOAT64 Description: Worked at Home. The count within a geographical area of workers over the age of 16 who worked at home.
Column name: workers_16_and_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers over the Age of 16. The number of people in each geography who work. Workers include those employed at private for-profit companies, the self-employed, government workers and non-profit employees.
Column name: associates_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population Completed Associate's Degree. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who obtained a associate's degree, and did not complete a more advanced degree.
Column name: bachelors_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population Completed Bachelor's Degree. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who obtained a bachelor's degree, and did not complete a more advanced degree.
Column name: high_school_diploma Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population Completed High School. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who completed high school, and did not complete a more advanced degree.
Column name: less_one_year_college Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population completed less than one year of college, no degree. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who attended college for less than one year and no further.
Column name: masters_degree Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population Completed Master's Degree. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who obtained a master's degree, but did not complete a more advanced degree.
Column name: one_year_more_college Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population completed more than one year of college, no degree. The number of people in a geographic area over the age of 25 who attended college for more than one year but did not obtain a degree
Column name: pop_25_years_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population 25 Years and Over. The number of people in a geographic area who are over the age of 25.  This is used mostly as a denominator of educational attainment.
Column name: commute_35_44_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute between 35 and 44 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in between 35 and 44 minutes. 
Column name: commute_60_more_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with a commute of over 60 minutes. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in over 60 minutes.
Column name: commute_less_10_mins Type: FLOAT64 Description: Number of workers with less than 10 minute commute. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home and commute in less than 10 minutes.
Column name: commuters_16_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Workers age 16 and over who do not work from home. The number of workers in a geographic area over the age of 16 who do not work from home
Column name: hispanic_any_race Type: FLOAT64 Description: Hispanic of any race
Column name: pop_5_years_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population 5 Years and Over. The number of people in a geographic area who are over the age of 5.  This is primarily used as a denominator of measures of language spoken at home.
Column name: speak_only_english_at_home Type: FLOAT64 Description: Speaks only English at Home. The number of people in a geographic area over age 5 who speak only English at home.
Column name: speak_spanish_at_home Type: FLOAT64 Description: Speaks Spanish at Home. The number of people in a geographic area over age 5 who speak Spanish at home, possibly in addition to other languages.
Column name: speak_spanish_at_home_low_english Type: FLOAT64 Description: Speaks Spanish at Home, speaks English less than "very well"
Column name: do_date Type: STRING Description: None
Column name: pop_15_and_over Type: FLOAT64 Description: Population 15 Years and Over. The number of people in a geographic area who are over the age of 15.  This is used mostly as a denominator of marital status.
Column name: pop_never_married Type: FLOAT64 Description: Never Married. The number of people in a geographic area who have never been married.
Column name: pop_now_married Type: FLOAT64 Description: Currently married. The number of people in a geographic area who are currently married
Column name: pop_separated Type: FLOAT64 Description: Married but separated. The number of people in a geographic area who are married but separated
Column name: pop_widowed Type: FLOAT64 Description: Widowed. The number of people in a geographic area who are widowed
Column name: pop_divorced Type: FLOAT64 Description: Divorced. The number of people in a geographic area who are divorced
